1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,414
You packed the water. The school chat changes the time.

2
00:00:03,414 --> 00:00:06,146
Then cancels the trip. What still needs doing?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,169
What still needs doing? And what can you stop worrying

4
00:00:11,169 --> 00:00:11,485
about?

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,209
Paste a chat about one event. Give its message date

6
00:00:18,209 --> 00:00:21,418
if known. Tomorrow Ready turns the conversation into a plan

7
00:00:21,418 --> 00:00:22,381
you can review.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,086
The fictional chat is Ukrainian. The form is due today

9
00:00:28,086 --> 00:00:31,172
at eight p.m. The trip is tomorrow at eight twenty.

10
00:00:31,172 --> 00:00:34,258
Water and a raincoat are required. The toy question is

11
00:00:34,258 --> 00:00:34,567
excluded.

12
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,269
You returned the form and packed the water. Mark both

13
00:00:40,269 --> 00:00:43,537
done. The raincoat becomes the next step. No second account

14
00:00:43,537 --> 00:00:44,191
is needed.

15
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,021
Now the school moves the meeting to eight oh five.

16
00:00:50,021 --> 00:00:53,043
This message changes only the time. It does not list

17
00:00:53,043 --> 00:00:54,251
the packing items again.

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,954
Attach the update to the same event. Review the time

19
00:01:02,954 --> 00:01:06,908
replacement. The app keeps the form, water, and raincoat requirements.

20
00:01:06,908 --> 00:01:10,862
Your completed work stays checked. Confirm after reviewing the change.

21
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,914
The updated plan explains the difference. The meeting is earlier.

22
00:01:16,914 --> 00:01:20,827
Your completed work survives. The next step remains finding the

23
00:01:20,827 --> 00:01:21,218
raincoat.

24
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,234
Then the chat says the trip is cancelled. The app

25
00:01:26,234 --> 00:01:29,467
proposes the exact statement, with the sender and time still

26
00:01:29,467 --> 00:01:32,054
attached. A question or rumour is not enough.

27
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,577
The app proposes the exact cancellation quotation. It has not

28
00:01:38,577 --> 00:01:42,154
applied the cancellation yet. The parent checks the event and

29
00:01:42,154 --> 00:01:45,731
confirms the scope. An empty model answer alone cannot cancel

30
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:46,446
the plan.

31
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,433
Now the app says no preparation is needed for this

32
00:01:52,433 --> 00:01:55,866
event. Those active tasks leave the list. Other event plans

33
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:56,553
remain unchanged.

34
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,580
If cancellation was a mistake, restore the previous version. The

35
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:06,160
earlier meeting time returns. The form and water stay done.

36
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:08,308
You do not rebuild your plan.

37
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,082
Meta Muse Spark Open interprets the language through Fireworks. Local

38
00:02:13,082 --> 00:02:17,165
quotation and date checks validate the draft. Our revision logic

39
00:02:17,165 --> 00:02:21,247
preserves state, and the parent approves changes. This separation makes

40
00:02:21,247 --> 00:02:22,472
the result inspectable.

41
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,845
The source includes regression tests and a key-free replay. This

42
00:02:26,845 --> 00:02:30,690
edited video uses recorded responses to fictional messages. It does

43
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:32,997
not simulate a live response speed.

44
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,193
This is a focused prototype. Model output still needs review.

45
00:02:39,193 --> 00:02:43,386
Broad real-world accuracy and independent parent acceptance remain unproven. We

46
00:02:43,386 --> 00:02:45,482
make no measured time-saving claim.

47
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,584
For this prototype, the promise is focused: one parent, one

48
00:02:49,584 --> 00:02:53,167
event, a plan that survives change. Keep what is done.

49
00:02:53,167 --> 00:02:56,392
See what is different. Know what to do next.
